 "corrections": [
  {
   "spec": "G3",
   "what": "G3 lists live.abdm.gov.in for the production sessions URL; G2/CORE give apis.abdm.gov.in/api/hiecm/gateway/v3/sessions. Used G2 (config is the single source of defaults).",
   "source": "G2 ENV table, CORE.md"
  },
  {
   "spec": "G4",
   "what": "G4 gives apis.abdm.gov.in/pmjay/hcx as production registry base; G2 gives apisprod.nha.gov.in/pmjay/hcx/participanthcxservice. Used G2.",
   "source": "G2 ENV table"
  },
  {
   "spec": "G8",
   "what": "G8D prose says an unmatched message writes no row, but the G8 pseudocode/table record it as delivered. Followed the pseudocode: every inbound is recorded (status delivered, peer.outcome=unmatched).",
   "source": "G8 pseudocode"
  },
  {
   "spec": "G8",
   "what": "Inbound also accepts a flattened JWE (protected/encrypted_key/iv/ciphertext/tag) and cleartext type:ProtocolResponse bodies (payloadType protocol).",
   "source": "nhcx-docs MCP (protocol error responses)"
  },
  {
   "spec": "G2",
   "what": "Keys starting with $comment are allowed anywhere in the config so the example file can document every key; all other unknown keys are still rejected.",
   "source": "implementation decision"
  },
  {
   "spec": "G1",
   "what": "In CARE the G1 background loops run as Celery beat tasks (care.nhcx.tasks.refresh_tokens every 60 s, prune_ledger hourly, check_gateway on worker_ready), only where settings.NHCX_ROLE is true. Gateway.start()/stop() keep the thread loops for hosts without Celery.",
   "source": "SCAFFOLDING 7, task brief"
  },
  {
   "spec": "G7",
   "what": "send() refuses to run inside a caller's atomic block (SendInTransactionError, a RuntimeError, not a SendError); atomic blocks opened by Django TestCase (_from_testcase) are ignored so services stay testable.",
   "source": "SCAFFOLDING 8"
  },
  {
   "spec": "G9",
   "what": "Ledger is safe across processes (gunicorn workers + celery): an fcntl lock on <dir>/.lock around id allocation and writes, and each reader refreshes its in-memory index incrementally from <day>/index.jsonl before queries.",
   "source": "implementation decision (multi-process deployment)"
  },
  {
   "spec": "G3",
   "what": "Session tokens are also shared through Django's default cache (settings.NHCX_SHARED_TOKEN_CACHE, default true) so the refresher process warms tokens for web workers.",
   "source": "implementation decision"
  },
  {
   "spec": "G5",
   "what": "x-hcx-timestamp and the acceptance timestamp use the Django time zone (Asia/Kolkata in CARE) rather than the container's process zone; @hcx suffix detection is case-insensitive.",
   "source": "implementation decision"
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "Public surface: care.nhcx.gateway.get_gateway() -> Gateway (raises GatewayNotConfigured, code NOT_CONFIGURED; a failed open is retried at most every 60 s); gateway_status() -> (Gateway|None, cause|None); set_gateway(gw)/reset_gateway() for tests.",
  "Send: get_gateway().send(path: str, envelope: dict) -> SendResult(ok, path, url, headers, gateway_status, response, duration_ms, ledger_id, txn_id, correlation_id, api_call_id, request_id; .error_code/.error_message when ok is false; .to_dict()). Raises SendError(code, message, retryable, upstream_status, upstream_body, ledger_id/txn_id, correlation_id, api_call_id, request_id, headers; .to_dict()) and SendInTransactionError. ok=false (NHCX answered non-2xx) is a result, not an exception. care.nhcx.gateway.send is the G7 module, there is no package-level send function.",
  "Envelope keys: fhir (or payload; object or JSON string), jwe_headers, any x-hcx-* key, and aliases sender, recipient, correlation_id, request_id, api_call_id, workflow_id, status.",
  "Ledger (gw.ledger): related(txn_id) -> [Row]; fhir(txn_id) -> {meta:{type,payloadType,path,time}, jwe_headers, fhir}; dispatch(txn_id) -> {txnId, status: dispatched|dispatch_failed|<raw>, errorCode?, errorMessage?}; list(limit=200) -> [Row] newest first; get(id) -> full entry dict | None; thread(correlation_id) -> dict|None. Row = {id, direction, status, sender, recipient, correlation_id, api_call_id, type, flow, created_at}. Errors are GatewayError with code NO_TXN_ID, TXN_NOT_FOUND, LEDGER_DISABLED, LEDGER_CORRUPT.",
  "Beneficiary: gw.beneficiary.policies_search(query: dict) -> {status: int, body: parsed JSON or {error: text}}; query keys identifiertype/identifiervalue, or mobile, or abhaNo; raises GatewayError NO_IDENTIFIER. Also abha_link(body), abha_delink(body).",
  "Tokens: gw.token(participant=None, refresh=False) -> {token, token_type, expires_at, expires_in, participant}; gw.refresh_token(participant).",
  "C1 contract: receive(envelope, delivery) where envelope={meta:{type:'in',payloadType,path,ip,time,redelivery,participant}, jwe_headers, fhir} and delivery={path,type,flow,payload_kind,correlation_id,api_call_id,redelivery,participant}; return 'settled'|'unmatched'|'ignored'|'rejected' (string, enum with .value, or {outcome, detail}); anything else or an exception gives 502 RECEIVE_FAILED so NHCX redelivers. Resolved lazily from settings.NHCX_RECEIVE_HANDLER; when not importable every message is answered unmatched.",
  "Routes (root and /api/gateway/): POST /in/<path>, POST /v1/<rest>, GET|POST /healthz, GET|POST /in/healthz, GET /readyz. Not-configured: inbound answers 202 unmatched, readyz 503.",
  "No code commits were made by this agent (coordinator commits)."
 ]
